{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1386860-here-s-some-interesting-news","id":1386860,"title":"Here's Some Interesting News","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T19:03:06-07:00","id":1386860,"title":"Here's Some Interesting News","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1255879159701811203\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EW3G7DTWkAAaSB-?format=webp&amp;name=large\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1255879159701811203\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness (@worldofdarkness) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1255879159701811203\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1255879159701811203 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In Vampire: The Masquerade - Out for Blood, you play as a hunter protecting your small town against the bloodsuckers. Study their ways and exploit their rivalries, or you'll become a vampire yourself! Wishlist it here: https://t.co/rdEypKq9Ko </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T10:17:10-07:00","id":1387293,"title":"","content":"Figures we'd get that instead of ever seeing a proper Vigil game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T10:36:15-07:00","id":1387295,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't expect any Chronicles of Darkness licensed games out of Paradox when they've been open and consistent about pushing the World of Darkness license. They want the products they license out to succeed, and they're pursuing a strategy of brand recognition where having the World of Darkness name out on different products is supposed to bolster interest. Putting out Of Darkness games that aren't from their Of Darkness line is brand dilution. I'm not saying this is good, but it's business and it's no surprise.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't read too deep into this game. It's one of three simultaneous announcements of licensed visual novels by a studio that does a ton of low-cost visual novels. That's not to imply that the writers and developers aren't trying to make a good and worthwhile product, but this is maybe around the midpoint on the high/low profile spectrum between VTM: Bloodlines 2 and World of Darkness licensed slot machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},